// Curved fjc>1 EXCESS-COLUMN regression (ref 21 Aug 2026, the
// measure-consistency fix): theta_exc + the four moment columns for
// adsorption FROM SOLUTION (phibulk != 0) on a spherical FJC_choices 5
// (fjc = 2) lattice -- the class every earlier curved-fjc test was
// structurally blind to (all were pinned/grafted, phibulk = 0, or had no
// excess columns). Guards the 21 Aug 2026 fix: theta_exc subtracts
// phibulk in the lattice's OWN measure L_sum = sum(L[iv]), not the
// geometric closed-form volume. On curved fjc>1 lattices the refined
// shells are bond-thick smears whose sum EXCEEDS the geometric volume by
// a surface term (~2 pi R^2/fjc; here L_sum = 67452.6 vs V = 65449.8,
// 3.06%), and the old geometric-volume subtraction polluted every excess
// and moment column by phibulk*(L_sum - V) = 40.1 of the reported 53.3
// -- the "mean position" 1.31 sat physically inside the frozen core
// (radius 3). SELF-VALIDATING at creation: kal theta_exc ==
// sum((phi-phibulk)*L) and the moments == their L-measure integrals from
// the committed .pro at machine precision; a UNIFORM bulk now has
// exactly ZERO excess (tests/manual/curved_fjc_excess.py); theta_exc and
// <z> are fjc-CONSISTENT (theta_exc 11.99/13.24, <z> 5.57/5.26 at
// fjc 1/2, converging on the physical-shell values 12.18/5.20).
// INTENTIONALLY DEVIATES from the compiled Namics, which mixes the
// measures the same old way (oracle on this input: theta_exc 53.2975,
// 1st_M 1.3076 -- matching the polluted values to 3e-9 was
// bug-compatibility, namics_bugs_overview #29; its 2nd_M additionally
// misses the *fjc compensation, #28). fjc = 1 and planar and all
// phibulk = 0 cases are bit-identical to before the fix. Full diagnosis:
// doc/fjc_offset_volume_notes.md.
lat : NN : n_layers : 25
lat : NN : geometry : spherical
lat : NN : lattice_type : hexagonal
lat : NN : FJC_choices : 5

mon : S : freedom : frozen
mon : S : frozen_range : 1;3
mon : A : freedom : free
mon : A : chi_S : -1.5
mon : A : chi_W : 0.4
mon : W : freedom : free

mol : pol : composition : (A)25
mol : pol : freedom : free
mol : pol : phibulk : 0.02

mol : W : composition : (W)1
mol : W : freedom : solvent

newton : NN : tolerance : 1e-8

output : kal : append : false
kal : mon : A : theta_exc
kal : mon : A : 1st_M_phi_z
kal : mon : A : 2nd_M_phi_z
kal : mon : A : RMS
kal : mon : A : fluctuations
kal : mol : pol : theta_exc

output : pro : append : false
pro : mon : A : phi

start
